This folder contains Android bindings based on the java-jni bindings.

The first step to building these bindings is to build the java-jni/
bindings.  These bindings use code generated from there.
See the ../java-jni README before continuing.

There is an Android Studio project here under SWORD/

This Android Studio project should be used to build the NDK
native code here.

After that, a make in this folder will copy the native libs
to the ../cordova/ bindings to produce a working cordova plugin

The steps to build all of this are usually:
1) make in the ../java-jni bindings folder
2) build all in SWORD Android Studio project
3) a make in this folder, which finally copies the binary libs
	to the ../cordova/ bindings folder to produce a working
	cordova plugin

Android java bindings can be used after step 2
cordova javascript bindings can be used after step 3

Hope this helps get you started.  Let me know your progress!

OpenSSL and curl
----------------
libsword links libcurl, which links OpenSSL.  Both used to come from
Google's com.android.ndk.thirdparty prefab packages, but Google stopped
publishing those in 2022 (curl 7.85, OpenSSL 1.1.1q: end-of-life and
4 KB page-aligned only).  We now build them ourselves with Google's
ndkports tooling and the same NDK the bindings use, so every .so in the
plugin is 16 KB page-aligned (required for Android 15+ devices).

The build recipe (as of 2026-09-04, OpenSSL 3.5.8 LTS and curl 8.22.0):

  git clone https://android.googlesource.com/platform/tools/ndkports
  # drop the release tarballs in as openssl/src.tar.gz and curl/src.tar.gz,
  # set portVersion in each build.gradle.kts, group org.crosswire.ndkports,
  # add -Wl,-z,max-page-size=16384 (OpenSSL Configure arg, curl LDFLAGS),
  # OpenSSL 3 wants ANDROID_NDK_ROOT; curl 8 wants --with-openssl and
  # --without-libpsl.  Gradle 7.5 there needs JDK 11; OpenSSL's Configure
  # needs the perl FindBin, IPC::Cmd and Time::Piece modules (dnf: perl-FindBin
  # perl-IPC-Cmd perl-Time-Piece).
  ./gradlew -PndkPath=$ANDROID_HOME/ndk/<version> -Prelease \
      :openssl:distZip :curl:distZip

The resulting build/repository trees (AAR + POM) are published, like the
Apple dependencies, on crosswire.org:

  https://crosswire.org/ftpmirror/pub/sword/dependencies/android/prefab/
  (the ndkports patch and the source tarballs sit beside it)

SWORD/build.gradle lists that URL as a Maven repository, after a local
prefab-repo/ directory here for anyone rebuilding the ports themselves,
and SWORD/app/build.gradle names the versions.
